Z||000000||David DeVoe||09-02-2001||12:08 PM||||Just looked carefully at the new cam bearings in my remanned 2.8. I'm new to this engine and clueless except I have a copy of Tom Currao's book. Looking at the #1 bearing I noticed a notch starting at the oil hole and going to the forward edge of the bearing. It seems to be perfectly square bottomed so it is not a scratch, but seems to be put there on purpose. My question is is this notch supposed to be there, is it the wrong bearing, or did the machinist make it when he pressed the bearing in. I NEED to know before I can even think about putting the cam in. Thanks for any help<BR>Dave||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||09-02-2001||12:27 PM||||Hey Dave!<BR>The notch is only in the #1 position, correct?<BR>It is to provide lube to the cam gear...<BR>It should not be on any other bearing...<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||David DeVoe||09-02-2001||02:32 PM||||Yes, only on the #1 bearing; it goes from one of the oil holes out towards the chain case. What you say makes sense. Have you seen this first hand?? No mention is made of this notch in any of the literature I have.<BR>Thanks <BR>Dave||||reg||1
